{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For two acute angles,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>cos</mi>\n\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mi>Q</mi>\n\t\t</mfenced>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>sin</mi>\n\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t\t</mfenced>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The measures, in degrees, of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are <math alttext=\"x plus 52\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>52</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"4 x plus 13\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>13</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, respectively. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["8bcf6063-6714-484c-a629-82b4e3ee15a6"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "8bcf6063-6714-484c-a629-82b4e3ee15a6", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "245c0b4f-83cc-4ff7-a238-241082f0fdd1", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "12c2fe00-bb06-4941-be9b-e94ff8a197eb", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "c167a1e8-3a2a-4473-80e4-a61f28f55279", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"38\"><mn>38</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that for two acute angles, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. For two acute angles, if the sine of one angle is equal to the cosine of the other, the angles are complementary. Therefore, the sum of the measures, in degrees, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measures, in degrees, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus 52\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>52</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x plus 13\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></math>, respectively. Therefore,&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 52 right parenthesis plus left parenthesis 4 x plus 13 right parenthesis equals 90\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>52</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Combining like terms in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x plus 65 equals 90\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"65\"><mn>65</mn></math> from each side of this equation results in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 25\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 5\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This would be the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> were congruent rather than complementary.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "a3d7bd43-4b60-4b1e-a039-96f3769a34f2", "correct_answer": ["A"]}